CORE
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ default argument constructs the class being defined: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ default argument names a later static member: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ default arguments naming the class template's parameter: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
is unknown$
dropped the body
--
N5008 [class.mem.general]/7-8: a default argument in a class's
member-specification is a complete-class context.  Checking it while the class
was still being defined failed on `= path()` (the class's own constructor) and
on `= _S_default` (a static member declared further down), which aborted the
rest of the class body: every later member -- data members included -- was
unknown, and each method referring to one was dropped.  This is libstdc++'s
std::filesystem::path (`replace_extension(const path & = path())').
